+# TimeTracker Contract
+
+## API Surface
+
+### `TimeTracker` class
+
+```typescript
+class TimeTracker {
+  constructor(options?: { file?: string });
+  start(taskName: string): TimeEntry;
+  stop(): TimeEntry;
+  getLog(options?: { since?: Date }): TimeEntry[];
+  getSummary(): Record<string, number>;
+  getActiveTask(): { taskName: string } | null;
+}
+```
+
+### `TimeEntry` interface
+
+```typescript
+interface TimeEntry {
+  taskName: string;
+  startTime: string;  // ISO 8601
+  endTime?: string;    // ISO 8601
+}
+```
+
+## Behaviors
+
+### Core Operations
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 1 | `start(name)` creates an active entry with start time set to now | Call `start('test')`, verify returned entry has `taskName === 'test'` and `startTime` is a valid ISO date string, and no `endTime` |
+| 2 | `stop()` sets end time on the active entry | Call `start('test')`, call `stop()`, verify returned entry has `endTime` set to a valid ISO date string |
+| 3 | Starting a new timer auto-stops the previous one | Call `start('a')`, call `start('b')`, verify the entry for 'a' has an `endTime` set |
+| 4 | `stop()` when nothing is running throws an error | Call `stop()` on a fresh tracker, verify it throws |
+
+### Query Operations
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 5 | `getLog()` returns all entries | Start 2 tasks (stop between), call `getLog()`, verify 2 entries returned |
+| 6 | `getLog({ since })` filters entries starting on or after that date | Create entry with old startTime, create entry with recent startTime, call `getLog({ since: recentDate })`, verify only recent entry returned |
+| 7 | `getLog({ since })` includes running entries started before the since date | Create a running entry (no stop) started before `since`, call `getLog({ since })`, verify the running entry is included |
+| 8 | `getSummary()` returns object keyed by task name with total duration in ms | Start 'task1', stop after delay, call `getSummary()`, verify result has `task1` key with positive number |
+| 9 | `getSummary()` combines multiple entries for the same task name | Create 2 entries for 'task1' with known durations, call `getSummary()`, verify `task1` sum equals the two durations added |
+| 10 | `getActiveTask()` returns current task or null | Call `getActiveTask()` with no running task → null; start a task, call `getActiveTask()` → returns `{ taskName: '...' }` |
+
+### Persistence
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 11 | Persists data across instances | Create tracker A, start+stop a task, create tracker B with same file path, call `getLog()`, verify the entry exists |
+| 12 | Creates the data file if it does not exist | Use a path that doesn't exist, create tracker, start a task, verify file exists after |
+| 13 | File path is configurable | Pass `{ file: '/tmp/custom-path.json' }`, verify data is written there |
+
+### Edge Cases
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 14 | `start('')` with empty name throws | Call `start('')`, verify it throws |
+| 15 | Supports unicode task names | Call `start('🔥測試🌟')`, call `stop()`, verify entry stored and retrieved correctly |
+| 16 | `getLog({ since: futureDate })` returns empty array | Use a date far in the future, verify empty array |
+| 17 | `getLog({ since: oldDate })` returns all entries | Use a very old date (epoch), verify all entries returned |
+| 18 | `getSummary()` with no entries returns `{}` | Fresh tracker, call `getSummary()`, verify `{}` |
+| 19 | `getLog()` with no entries returns `[]` | Fresh tracker, call `getLog()`, verify `[]` |
+| 20 | Rapid sequential start calls do not corrupt data | Call `start('a')`, `start('b')`, `start('c')` in rapid succession, verify all 3 entries exist with correct task names |
+
+### Data Integrity
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 21 | Multiple start/stop cycles accumulate correctly | Do 5 start/stop cycles, verify 10 entries exist (5 for each variation) |
+| 22 | Log entries have correct shape | Verify each entry has `taskName` (string), `startTime` (string ISO), and optionally `endTime` |
+| 23 | Summary durations are positive numbers | Start a task, wait 1ms, stop, verify `getSummary()` has positive values |
+| 24 | `stop()` returns the stopped entry | `start('x')`, `const e = stop()`, verify `e.taskName === 'x'` and `e.endTime` is set |
+| 25 | Auto-stop returns the new entry and previous task is stopped | `start('a')`, `const e = start('b')`, verify `e.taskName === 'b'`, and calling `getLog()` shows entry 'a' has endTime |
